  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string S0S_0S0​ of length NNN consisting of lowercase english alphabets.\n\nWe define the string Si=S(i−1)+S_i = S_{(i-1)} +Si​=S(i−1)​+ `reverse`(S(i−1))(S_{(i-1)})(S(i−1)​), where `reverse`(X)(X)(X) denotes the string obtained after reversing the string XXX.\n\nGiven an integer KKK, find the number of times S0S_0S0​ appears as a **substring** in SKS_KSK​.\n\nSince the answer can be huge, print it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK — the length of initial string and the number of operations.\nThe next line contains a string of length NNN consisting of lowercase english alphabets.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the number of times S0S_0S0​ appears as a **substring** in SKS_KSK​.\nSince the answer can be huge, print it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤N≤106",
      "1≤K≤1091 \\leq K \\leq 10^91≤K≤109",
      "S0S_0S0​ consists of lowercase english alphabets only.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1062\\cdot 10^62⋅106."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4 2\ncode\n2 3\naa\n7 3\nracecar",
        "output": "2\n15\n8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Given S0=S_0 =S0​= code.\n\nS1=S_1=S1​= codeedoc.\nS2=S_2=S2​= codeedoccodeedoc.\n\nTotal number of substrings in S2=S_2=S2​= codeedoccodeedoc that match S0=S_0=S0​= code is 222.\nTest case 222: Given S0=S_0 =S0​= aa.\n\nS1=S_1=S1​= aaaa.\nS2=S_2=S2​= aaaaaaaa.\nS3=S_3=S3​= aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa.\n\nTotal number of substrings in SK=S_K=SK​= aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa that match S0=S_0=S0​= aa is 151515.\nTest case 333: Given S0=S_0=S0​= racecar. S3S_3S3​ will be racecarracecarracecarracecarracecarracecarracecarracecar.\nTotal number of substrings in SKS_KSK​ that match S0S_0S0​ is 888."
      }
    ]
